.TH  ENVMGR  1 2/21/92
.CM 4
.SH NAME
envmgr \- Environment Manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBenvmgr\fP [\fB-d\fP] [\fB-N hashtablesize\fP]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fIenvmgr(1)\fR implements the environment service.
.PP
\fIenvmgr\fR interprets the following options:
.TP 8
.B \-d
Turns on debugging.  \fIenvmgr\fR will print informative messages
to stderr whenever something happens.
.TP 8
.B \-N hashtablesize
Sets the size of the hash table where ports are kept (internal). The default
is 500 which should be enough.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.I "MACH Environment Manager,"
Mary Thompson, Carnegie Mellon University, 1989
